      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SNOBBERY (5) gets the nod on exposed recent form despite being beaten as favourite at Gawler last start, where he was fourth over 1719m and only fair to the line. His previous run when fresh was better than it suggests, and third-up he looks well placed to break through. THE PUNK ROCKER (6) is the main danger. His fourth here two back when beaten a length at big odds reads well for a race of this shape and out in trip can threaten. ELROND (1) has been sixth at his past two Gawler runs, beaten within two and a half lengths in both. Well placed and in the mix if the quick back-up suits. MAJESTIC MOSHE (3) was out of the money two runs back when fresh from a spell then again missed the frame last start over 1400m at this track. Fitter and best efforts measure up so worth another chance.",
